{"title":"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Induction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Induction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a finite set of points in three-dimensional space.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a5f9f8ccf65788910b19a2839fcaf33c9bb5280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e608b1893da6f78192d510382177e4ea2e168ba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"21\" height=\"19\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9be2cd185e62f12516b30b3454efbce434a009f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, be the sets consisting of the orthogonal projections of the points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> onto the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />-plane, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4298cac30b507b9b11e913877499d5dc473fe448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$zx$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />-plane, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-plane, respectively.  Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b8ce4523020572a5cdf3349b8b11c1a428dce77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|S|^{2} \\le |S_{x}| \\cdot |S_{y}| \\cdot |S_{z}|,\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7ded470c5c84305a67acacfe0ff329cf6c4597be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the number of elements in the finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7ded470c5c84305a67acacfe0ff329cf6c4597be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. (Note: The orthogonal projection of a point onto a plane is the foot of the perpendicular from that point to the plane)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4871a6ebec4c21e536ae11d1d6f66674cd6f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be planes with index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> that are parallel to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-plane that contain multiple points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> on those planes such that all points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are distributed throughout all planes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4871a6ebec4c21e536ae11d1d6f66674cd6f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> according to their <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-coordinates in common.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a772bd794fbedb2976268c491686644aefc02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of unique projected points from each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4871a6ebec4c21e536ae11d1d6f66674cd6f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />-plane\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c12f232787a76f7499dacc975199ddfb05bf02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> be the number of unique projected points from each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4871a6ebec4c21e536ae11d1d6f66674cd6f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd70347c7940f63ff9417e383548564fd92aff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" />-plane\n</p><p>This provides the following: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04be466354326922fce0666d20393538df9203c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_{i}| \\le a_{i}b_{i}\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> [Equation 1]\n</p><p>We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a41ce9539b2c094dd40792bddf7679ec0c84922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}|Z_{i}|\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"110\" height=\"53\" /> [Equation 2]\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a772bd794fbedb2976268c491686644aefc02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of unique projected points from each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4871a6ebec4c21e536ae11d1d6f66674cd6f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />-plane,\n</p><p>if we add them together it will give us the total points projected onto the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />-plane.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e05d8ad2733b882aa6f3e3ea324c10bf48406c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_{x}|=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"105\" height=\"53\" /> [Equation 3]\n</p><p>likewise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268f0de087e24f60917d3b820c9a0123aca73ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_{y}|=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"102\" height=\"53\" /> [Equation 4]\n</p><p>We also know that the total number of elements of each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4871a6ebec4c21e536ae11d1d6f66674cd6f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> is less or equal to the total number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9be2cd185e62f12516b30b3454efbce434a009f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c803126d5a3a3a5ce744611383cdce46c3ded720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_{i}| \\le |S_{z}|\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> [Equation 5]\n</p><p>Multiplying [Equation 1] by [Equation 5] we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa0c7148c6c762d2dc79e8b5fefed10db81144cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_{i}|^{2} \\le a_{i}b_{i}|S_{z}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b656b10a454070601b0b040f54a5fceb55b0fec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_{i}| \\le \\sqrt{a_{i}b_{i}}\\sqrt{|S_{z}|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Adding all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5efe1a903937a962916d27ca0d5bdf3e7a3f9d64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_{i}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c05aa19c8a3c55578acc6604a1c00341831274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}|Z_{i}| \\le \\sqrt{|S_{z}|}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sqrt{a_{i}b_{i}}\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"212\" height=\"53\" />[Equation 6]\n</p><p>Substituting [Equation 2] into [Equation 6] we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47ba12aba4761d234ee8c3d31bd5b137edd1dfed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S| \\le \\sqrt{|S_{z}|}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sqrt{a_{i}b_{i}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"173\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a5c162c95c524e38e9ac3c48497e0c7e97166c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|^{2} \\le |S_{z}| \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sqrt{a_{i}b_{i}} \\right)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"198\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Since, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/9933dda6591420a664fbcc8aa7ce75a32b7fc26b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sqrt{a_{i}b_{i}} \\le \\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}}\\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"224\" height=\"67\" />,\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a96df9416eec19b97bee59c6a43d8243c441863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|^{2} \\le |S_{z}| \\left( \\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}}\\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}} \\right)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"250\" height=\"71\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3acaf6767478802c68dfe05fd389b75cbaebcac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|^{2} \\le |S_{z}| \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\\right)\\left( \\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_{i}\\right)\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"238\" height=\"55\" /> [Equation 7]\n</p><p>Substituting [Equation 3] and [Equation 4] into [Equation 7] we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9acf4c5130272d7c0353070ec95819b0907ebb77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|^{2} \\le |S_{x}| \\cdot |S_{y}| \\cdot |S_{z}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"170\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28Induction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Induction)\">Solution 2(Induction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Induction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/112a2c619d2fe83912cbbf00684bc8c853dbc8c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1, z_2, \\dots, z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"11\" /> be the possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> - coordinates of the points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e6d4dd0b43c9ef571ddaaba7053eac0800e7c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i = \\{ (x,y,z) \\in S | z=z_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" /> be the set of points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/7532b41a34c9ca592694135d1de65eeb8d9ce036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cb26cc5d8bbbcde70d5f14bb1d9391b2ae729dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i =|\\{ y \\text{ there exist x  such that } (x, y, z_i) \\in S_i\\}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"357\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of points in the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />-plane\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b9a9994a9289e0f355078a1d53a00432f05d672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i =|\\{ x \\text{ there exist y  such that } (x, y, z_i) \\in S_i\\}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"356\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of points in the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd70347c7940f63ff9417e383548564fd92aff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" />-plane.\n</p><p><br />\nIt is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bed8d8dac13f2f031a24fcead248d3d382c3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_i|\\leq a_i\\cdot b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25cc89901516b5c6f3bc2c7bfdca54cb221a043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\max_{i=1}^n |S_i|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Induction Statement: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a735a00bf1536410e0d6d63d5c1f80232e5efa4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^k |S_i|\\right)^2 \\leq M \\sum_{i=1}^k a_i \\cdot \\sum_{i=1}^k b_i\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Base Case: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/0742bfa3801c35ab68aef94e62f00bca0f2e259b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_1|^2 \\leq M a_1 \\cdot b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" /> is trivial as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b1f3667d631b90291110b0893d7330494bc69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_i|\\leq a_1 \\cdot b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/70288b2196cff028cdda30bb3b708400ec05576a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_1|\\leq M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Induction Assumption (AI): Assume that statement is true for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a735a00bf1536410e0d6d63d5c1f80232e5efa4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^k |S_i|\\right)^2 \\leq M \\sum_{i=1}^k a_i \\cdot \\sum_{i=1}^k b_i\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Induction Step:\n</p><p>LHS:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k+1} |S_i|\\right)^2 &amp;= \\left(|S_{k+1}| + \\sum_{i=1}^{k} |S_i|\\right)^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k} |S_i|\\right)^2 + |S_{k+1}|^2 + 2\\cdot |S_{k+1}|\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k} |S_i|\\right)^2 \n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>RHS:\n\\begin{align*}\nM\\sum_{i=1}^{k+1}a_i \\sum_{i=1}^{k+1}b_i &amp;= M\\left(a_{k+1}+\\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_i\\right)\\left(b_{k+1}+\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right) \\\\ &amp;= M\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_i\\right)\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right) + M a_{k+1}b_{k+1} + Ma_{k+1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right)+Mb_{k+1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_i\\right)\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>By Induction assumption:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea31048648080165df0553421ba98e7ce534f3fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k} |S_i|\\right)^2 \\leq M\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_i\\right)\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right)\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Similarly to Base case\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947df7cec395521b93c6fc1d16b62376cfbd3d68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|S_{k+1}|^2 \\leq M a_{k+1}\\cdot b_{k+1}\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Using AM-GM we have \n\\begin{align*}\nMa_{k+1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right)+Mb_{k+1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_i\\right) &amp; \\geq 2\\sqrt{Ma_{k+1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right)\\cdot Mb_{k+1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_i\\right)} \\\\\n&amp;=2\\sqrt{M\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_i\\right)\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k} a_i\\right)}\n\\cdot \\sqrt {M a_{k+1}\\cdot b_{k+1}} \\\\\n&amp;\\text{ by Induction assumption and } |S_{k+1}|^2 \\leq M a_{k+1}\\cdot b_{k+1} \\\\ \n&amp;\\geq 2 |S_{k+1}| \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{k} |S_i|\\right) \n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>This proves the inductive claim.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> don't intersect and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/0806de84da40adce40209ae7e5a626d012e80d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\cup S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c09221c6960189738b5d902e74ea85c509a210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|=\\sum_{i=1}^n |S_i|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"104\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>To finish the proof observe that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/13048cc47733586817c9e632c45ead99cb7546b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i = |S_x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"100\" height=\"53\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1defffd0ad2119eff8cb7949f5abd4a0095ace4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n b_i=|S_y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"97\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f138bcbeb1b6ec3fbd682d96ddf617679e83aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\leq |S_z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO\" title=\"1992 IMO\">1992 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 418/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14413/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.597      1 Template:IMO_box\n